  "limitations": [
    "No new production candidate or additional matched speedup. Original loader and report/export comparisons measure different operations and cannot be combined into one generation speedup.",
    "GOMAXPROCS constrains Go scheduling, not CPU affinity or host-memory admission. These media backends have no general whole-request hard RAM/VRAM budget or resource-derived fallback planner. Physical allocation refusal is not successful lower-memory generation.",
    "Driver memory and counters belong to one library; process host peaks include earlier requests and construction. Whole-device free memory has a separate scope. CUDA admission waiting is excluded from per-request rows.",
    "SenseNova still constructs request-specific resident components and allocates about 33 GB on the Go heap per measured request. Retaining these components requires a distinct cache policy and comparison of retained VRAM, changed inputs and multi-model pressure; the cleanup fix does not eliminate this cost.",
    "The changed SenseNova request has repeat/fresh-session equivalence, not a new external pixel oracle or perceptual quality assessment. Prior frozen corpus visual limitations remain unchanged.",
    "Public API/browser behavior and final publication remain separate plan steps."
  ],
